<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Thy love, by man so sorely tried,</l><l>Proved stronger than the grave;</l><l>The very spear that pierced Thy side</l><l>Drew forth the blood to save;</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Though Thou didst pass through woes and grief,</l><l>Thy works were ever good;</l><l>Although midst sorrows all Thy life,</l><l>Thou spak’st no murmuring word.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Faithful amidst unfaithfulness,</l><l>’Mid darkness only light,</l><l>Thou didst Thy Father’s name confess,</l><l>And in His will delight;</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Unmoved by Satan’s subtle wiles,</l><l>Or suffering, shame, and loss,</l><l>Thy path, uncheered by earthly smiles,</l><l>Led only to the cross.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>We wonder at Thy lowly mind,</l><l>And fain would like Thee be,</l><l>And all our rest and pleasure find</l><l>In learning, Lord, of Thee.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
